1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,410
In Aramaic, "Barabbas" means "son of the father."

2
00:00:03,591 --> 00:00:05,212
He was a robber in prison.

3
00:00:05,212 --> 00:00:07,733
Pilate, the governor, offered to free one man.

4
00:00:08,641 --> 00:00:10,575
Pilate knew the leaders were jealous of Jesus.

5
00:00:11,394 --> 00:00:14,813
Barabbas, or Jesus which is called Christ?

6
00:00:15,465 --> 00:00:16,055
Barabbas.

7
00:00:17,102 --> 00:00:18,896
Why, what evil hath he done?

8
00:00:19,387 --> 00:00:20,440
Let him be crucified.

9
00:00:20,871 --> 00:00:22,920
Listen: Bar-ABBA.

10
00:00:25,089 --> 00:00:28,748
Jesus called God "Abba." It means Father.

11
00:00:28,976 --> 00:00:30,047
So the robber went free.

12
00:00:31,216 --> 00:00:33,331
The true Son of the Father did not.

13
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:34,913
Barabbas only had the name.

14
00:00:35,958 --> 00:00:38,402
Jesus died so we could call God Father too.
